# Your financial data. This is the important line in this file.
#
# data/ holds wallet.db -- every purchase, with dates, merchants and amounts --
# and fx_rates.csv, which is derived. Neither belongs in a repository, and the
# first one belongs in a public one least of all. If you add a feature that
# writes anything derived from a transaction, add it here in the same commit.
data/
*.db
*.csv

# ...except the sample, which is invented and is there so a clone has
# something to import.
!sample-statement.csv

# ...and except the rate history the published page ships, which is the one
# CSV here that is not yours. It is the ECB's own daily reference series --
# public data about the euro, with nothing in it derived from a transaction.
# The rule above exists to keep spending out of a public repository, and
# there is none in this file. Without this line the page would publish with
# its rate file silently missing and every conversion on it would fail.
!docs/app/fx_rates.csv

# ...and the pound wallet's own copy, for the same reason. It carries the CAD
# and GBP legs rather than CAD and USD, and it is the same public ECB series
# with nothing of yours in it. It lives under standalone/ rather than docs/
# because docs/ is what GitHub Pages publishes and that file is only ever a
# build input. Listed separately rather than widening the rule to a glob:
# these exceptions should stay a list somebody can read and check, because
# the cost of one wrong pattern here is publishing a ledger.
!standalone/pounds/fx_rates.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Test artefacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# Editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
